[OC]|cffffffffThe Altar of Zul|r  -  a troll ziggurat south-east, about 40 units. Come in from the north-west, kill the Vilebranch Axe Thrower on the lower slopes for the necklaces first, then climb, clear the Soothsayers on the stairs and touch the top. The DB puts two level 50 elites, Qiaga the Keeper and Morta'gya the Keeper, on the top beside the trigger: if they are there, do not pull them; step onto the trigger from the side away from them and leave. If they stand on the trigger itself, leave the step for now, finish the necklaces and Skulk Rock, and note it - the Altar is then a group step. |cFFFF0000Danger:|r Retherokk the Berserker (48, rare) stands at 50.5,64.1 on the east slope
Kill [TAR2639 Vilebranch Axe Thrower] (45-46) on the Altar's lower slopes for 5 Troll Tribal Necklaces [QC2880] (~30% - budget ~17 kills, fewer for every necklace from the cages); the Vilebranch Scalpers (~30%) and Soothsayers (~27%) there drop them too, but the Soothsayers on the stairs stand by the Keepers [G46.2,65.5 The Hinterlands]
Touch the top of the Altar of Zul (see the note above: never pull the Keepers) [QC2989] [G49.0,68.7 The Hinterlands]

[OC]|cffffffffSkulk Rock|r  -  north, about 25 units. Green Sludges (46-47) and Jade Oozes (47-48), none elite; the level 50 Green Sludges round the robot (around 46,37-40) are another creature and do not count. The DB also places level 50-51 dream creatures across Skulk Rock (Fallen Moonkin, Dreadfeather Hippogryphs, Wyrmkin Starhunters, Wrath Whelps; whether they are in the open world is |cffffcc00unverified|r): if they roam here, work the oozes on the west and south edge (x44-50 y45-55) and leave the rest
Kill 10 [TAR2655 Green Sludge] and 10 [TAR2656 Jade Ooze], sludges first [QC2877] [G51.7,44.5 The Hinterlands]
